<%# The whole wizard lives in one Turbo Frame: preview/apply POST back the full
    pasted text and render their step directly (the wizard is stateless, so a
    redirect can't carry the paste). Outside a frame Turbo Drive REJECTS
    non-redirect form responses and silently discards them — the buttons would
    do nothing. Inside the frame, direct renders are valid and turbo_confirm
    still works. %>
<%= turbo_frame_tag "reconcile" do %>
<p class="mb-3 text-gray-600">
  Import the monthly EUSA actuals sheet and reconcile it against submitted expenses
  and income budgets. Both the legacy format (Nominal, Cost Centre, Ref, …) and the Sage export
  (AccountNumber, …, GoodsValueInBaseCurrency) are accepted; the header identifies
  the columns automatically.
  <%= link_to "What the words mean", admin_reimbursements_glossary_path, class: "underline" %>.
</p>

<%# Where the sheet comes from. The page asked for "the monthly EUSA actuals
    sheet" and never said who sends it, how often, or what to do when it has
    not arrived — which for a successor is the difference between a monthly
    routine and a file they have never seen. %>
<%= render CardComponent.new(title: "Where this sheet comes from", html_class: "mb-4") do %>
  <p class="mb-0 text-sm text-gray-600">
    EUSA's finance office exports its ledger once a month and emails it out: one row per
    transaction that actually hit the account, for every cost centre. It lands weeks after the
    BACS run it confirms, so a claim sent to EUSA this week is normally reconciled next month.
    Upload the file as it arrived, or copy the rows out of Excel and paste them. If it has not
    come, ask EUSA's finance office for the latest actuals export; nothing here can fetch it.
  </p>
<% end %>

<% if flash[:alert].present? %>
  <%= render AlertComponent.new(type: :danger) do %><%= flash[:alert] %><% end %>
<% end %>

<%# multipart: true, or the browser posts the file's NAME and nothing else —
    `form_with url:` does not infer it from a file_field_tag the way the form
    builder's file_field does, and a request-level test never sees it because
    ActionController::TestCase bypasses form encoding entirely. Both import
    wizards already say it; this form did not. %>
<%= form_with url: preview_admin_reimbursements_reconciliation_path, method: :post,
              multipart: true do %>
  <%= render CardComponent.new(title: "Step 1: Paste actuals data") do |card| %>
    <% card.with_footer do %>
      <%= render "shared/form/actions", submit: "Parse and match" %>
    <% end %>

    <%# The upload half was never passed, so this was paste-only on the one
        screen whose input arrives as an email attachment. The file is turned
        into the same text a paste produces (ActualsUpload) before anything
        else sees it, so the two routes cannot give different answers. %>
    <%= render "shared/form/paste_or_upload",
          text_name: :pasted_text,
          text_label: "Actuals data (tab- or comma-separated, include the header row)",
          file_name: :actuals_file,
          file_label: "…or upload the sheet EUSA sent",
          file_accept: ::Reimbursements::ActualsUpload::ACCEPT,
          file_hint: "An .xlsx, .xls or .csv. Its first sheet is read, header row included.",
          text_value: @pasted_text, rows: 10,
          placeholder: "Nominal\tCost Centre\tRef\tDate\tPeriod\tNarrative\tNarrative 1\tDebit\tCredit\tNet",
          text_hint: "Each row's EUSA period (P1–P12) and cost centre are read from the pasted data, so " \
                     "there's no need to enter a month or pick a cost centre. A paste may cover several " \
                     "cost centres: each row is imported under its own, rows naming a cost centre that " \
                     "isn't set up here are skipped (and reported), and rows with no cost centre at all " \
                     "will ask you where they belong." %>
  <% end %>
<% end %>
<% end %>
